+Independent complete compatibility proof, 2026-10-08.
+
+Result and limits
+The reversed data profile9 singletons+21,17,481 remains compatible with
+L25=I+J and one generic rational first factor L23. All2300 actual second-axis
+triple lines satisfy the needed individual nonvanishing conditions. PR36's
+new rank-one center complements are also valid in this fixed basis. The
+complete original-envelope h25 internal profile must be freshly certified;
+its copied-center update removes25 identity width25 calls and adds25 rank-one
+calls, while preserving all rank24 copied transforms and their ACTUAL profiles.
+This proof establishes simultaneous geometry, not the full characteristic,
+assembly, physical producer replay or inherited fixed-tape theorem.
+
+Attribution
+PR34 (James Chang) supplies the reversed family; PR37 combines its23/25
+instance with PR36's copied retained centers (icekylinx). PR32 (icekylinx)
+supplies fixed I+J projectors and original-envelope profiling. The controlled
+basis, ordered climb, two-stage/copied-stream construction and semantic
+interfaces retain the full prior source credits. This note adds an exact
+compatibility proof for fixing the second factor of that combined family.
+
+1. Actual common family
+
+Let a=23,b=25,m=575,d=47 and I=(0,...,22). Keep the controlled permutations
+M_beta completing first-d labelsR=[I,22,I] and last-d inverse-column labels
+C=[I,0,I]. Keep these permutations fixed. The remaining family is
+ K=T_M(L23 tensor (I25+J25)), L23 in GL23(Q).
+The complete earlier exact reversed23 controls check every permutation,
+both full restriction trees and the actual contraction formulas below.
+
+For an actual triple indicator t and H=I-J/9, put phi=t^t H/2. Then
+ v=(I+J)t=t+3*1,
+ nu=phi(I+J)^-1=(t-10/[3(b+1)]*1)^t/2.
+At b25 every primal and dual coordinate is nonzero. The products are
+ v_j nu_j=68/39 on the triple and -5/26 elsewhere,
+whose sum3*(68/39)+22*(-5/26)=1. These values are derived anew at25;
+the former h47 constants fail this normalization and are a negative control.
+A subset weight is(136i-15j)/78; for0<=i<=3,0<=j<=22 it is zero/one only
+for the empty/full subset. We do not infer the prefix proof from that fact.
+
+The actual first23/last23 contraction of A tensor(v nu) equals
+ diag(v_i) A diag(nu_(j+2)). Thus every generic first-factor ordinary local
+profile and its auxiliary23-corner survive with nonzero fixed diagonal scales.
+The actual first25/last25 contraction of(p xi) tensor B equals
+ diag(p_(r_i)) B diag(xi_(c_j)),
+ r=(0,...,22,22,0), c=(22,0,0,...,22).
+It transfers the ACTUAL fixed profile of any second-factor transition B.
+The scales depend only on generic L23 coordinates; no generic L25 hypothesis
+is used. Taking B=I gives the auxiliary25-corner. Rank-one source fronts and
+corank-one growth fronts remain valid because their source-line coordinates
+are nonzero, with the usual extreme pivot and central identity block.
+
+2. Complete data nonvanishing certificate
+
+The actual null corner of(I-p xi) tensor(I-v nu) is, after nonzero separate
+row and column scalings,
+ M_ij=[R_i=C_j]/z_(R_i)+[beta_i=gamma_j]/w_(beta_i)-1,
+ z_r=p_r xi_r, w_t=v_t nu_t,
