+Fixed-L25 copied-center profile: independent arithmetic and transfer audit
+
+Verdict: the copied-center replacement is valid on the COMPLETE newly
+profiled original-envelope h25 transition multiset. It removes exactly25
+full-identity width25 calls and adds25 rank-one complement calls. All rank24
+center transforms remain, with their actual fixed-basis ordered profiles.
+The five-prime calculation has a deterministic rational CRT justification,
+not a probable-zero interpretation. The common GL23 physical-corner proof
+was subsequently inspected independently in Section5 below; no new kappa is
+proved by this audit alone.
+
+Scope and source binding
+The original-envelope producer uses the fresh PR36 base-two graph, not the
+historical base-four h25 graph or its counts. fixed25_copied_crt_audit.json
+hashes the actual fresh h25.bin, base-two producer record, completed profile,
+and full_profiles25.cpp. The latter was inspected against the previously
+reviewed full_profiles47.cpp: only dimension assertions/comments and output
+filename change; primes, denominator formulas, transition construction,
+cache invalidation and maximum-northeast-rank reconstruction are unchanged.
+The profiler does not read enlarged-positive labels into its frame formula.
+Those separate labels may justify other axes; they cannot replace h25's
+original envelopes in this particular fixed-profile certificate.
+
+1. Actual designated centers and full-profile accounting
+The parsed fresh DAG has h25,v2300,q6925,c45963. Its25 designated kind1
+terminal roots are distinct, each with one distinct common point, full
+25-coordinate cover and original-envelope rank24. Original matching has
+1589 joins and R=c+q-matches=51299. Its old histogram mass is1283675=
+25*51299+2*600. Both rank24 and rank25 histogram entries have multiplicity25.
+These are source counts, not constants borrowed from another h25 producer.
+
+The actual full transition constructor puts edge(0,root) and edge(0,I) for
+each kind1 output. The first is exactly the rank24 center projector; the
+second is a full identity. Matching modifies other physical occurrences
+before profiling but cannot remove a center's separate terminal identity:
+its donor roles are additions and terminal output-use vertices have no
+outgoing producer consumer. Every nonfull original-envelope frame has rank
+at most24. Hence the only full-rank identity transitions are these25 calls,
+confirmed by completed fixed blocks[25]=25. All other profiled matrices
+have rank<25 and cannot yield a width25 block.
+
+Apply PR36's general copied-center argument (see copied_center_schedule_audit.txt):
+forward original at F_U w supplies a transformed copy F_0 w to scatter and
+moves directly to F_F w. Reverse original advances to F_Uperp w and a copy
+supplies F_F w to scatter. These are identities for the entire arbitrary
+old dirty value w and preserve original cleanup endpoints. The copied
+rank24 residual is the SAME operator as the original center detour, in the
+same fixed physical basis, in the appropriate orientation. Do not replace
+that operator's profile by a generic rank24 profile. Only the old full
+identity25 becomes the complementary rank1 operation, which always costs
+one singleton with the retained compiler. Thus after full profiling:
+ blocks'[1]=blocks[1]+25; blocks'[25]=blocks[25]-25;
+ every other block count is unchanged.
+Weighted mass becomes1283075=25*51299+600. Local saving is600; replications
+must use actual N/v25 in the global list. All role volumes and N endpoint
+corrections remain charged. The argument is invariant under simultaneous
+address conjugation and axis reversal; it does not require L25 to be generic.
+The controls worker separately checks the GL23 scales and physical corners.
+
+2. Exact projector denominator and rank-four correction
+For H=I-J/9 and L=I+J, L^-1=I-J/26. An original envelope has common core C,
+c=|C| in{1,2}, outside set O, n=|O|, s=3-c. Columns e_j+1_C/s have Gram
+I+(c-1)J/s^2. Put d=s^2+(c-1)n, p=1_O, w0=1_C+3*1,
+z0=78*1_C-10*1. Direct multiplication of the inverse Gram matrix gives
+ L P_U L^-1=Delta_O+Z/D_actual,
+ D_actual=78*d,
+ Z=s*p*z0^t+78*s*w0*p^t+n*w0*z0^t-78*(c-1)*p*p^t.
+Its correction column space is contained in span(p,w0), so rank Z<=2.
+A source triple has correction rank1, denominator156, and numerator
+(t+3*1)(78*t-10*1)^t. Zero and identity have correction zero, denominator1.
+The dimension-specific uniform individual bounds are:
+ core1: D<=312, |Zij|<=7288;
+ core2: D<=1872, |Zij|<=6714;
+ source line: D<=156, |Zij|<=272.
+Our independent script checks all423 row/column membership-state and n
+combinations, including unrealizable combinations that only enlarge the
+bound. These are bounds on the correction, not the full matrix.
+
+For a nested difference P_B-P_A, outside masks are nested: core_B subset
+core_A and cover_A subset cover_B imply O_A subset O_B. Source masks are
+zero and full masks identity. Every admitted transition therefore has
+M=Delta+Z/D_actual with a zero/one diagonal mask, rank Z<=4,
+ D_actual<=Dmax=1872^2=3504384,
+ |Zij|<=Bmax=2*1872*7288=27286272.
+Use the PRODUCT of the actual two frame denominators when subtracting.
+Dmax is ONLY an upper bound, not a common denominator: actual denominator
+390 occurs and does not divide3504384. Substituting Dmax as a putative
+clearing denominator would invalidate the proof.
+
+3. All-minor CRT gate
+Expanding a k-square minor by correction/mask columns needs at most four
+correction columns. The mask columns force their rows; a j-square
+correction determinant is bounded by j! Bmax^j. Consequently
+ N_minor=D_actual^4*minor is an INTEGER with absolute value at most
+ sum(j=0..4) binom(25,j) j! Bmax^j Dmax^(4-j)
+ =169285850832223787888583699370868736 (118bits).
+The five Mersenne primes with exponents61,31,19,17,13 are independently
+proved prime by Lucas-Lehmer in the audit script. Their product is
+2787226284877333278295360123920236600238079 (141bits), strictly above
+the bound. Every individual frame denominator is at most1872<8191, so
+all such factors and their products are invertible modulo every prime.
+The script additionally checks gcd against every possible denominator.
+If all modular reductions vanish, their product divides bounded integer
+N_minor, forcing N_minor=0. A single nonzero modular minor proves rational
+nonvanishing. A factor of two is unnecessary because this certifies zero,
+not signed integer reconstruction.
+
+4. Ordered profile from all northeast ranks
+For every northeast rectangle, each modular rank is at most rational rank.
+A maximal nonzero rational minor cannot vanish modulo every chosen prime
+by the strict bound. Thus rank_Q(rectangle)=max_p rank_Fp(rectangle).
+Take the mixed two-dimensional differences of these MAXIMUM CORNER RANKS
+to recover the rational ordered pivots. Taking the union of modular pivot
+sets or only the maximum total rank is not valid. The script includes
+[[5,7],[0,0]] modulo5 and7 as a pivot-union negative control, and diag(5,7)
+as a control showing why a too-small prime product can miss rational rank.
+
+The profiler uses allfive primes on EVERY profiled transition of rank>2,
+except the exact full identity; ranks1/2 may conservatively remain singleton
+calls. If profiles agree, that profile already supplies all corner maxima.
+If they differ, its explicit northeast merge is necessary and valid. The
+initial first-prime rank assertion could abort on a bad prime but cannot
+produce a false successful certificate. Caches for participating frames
+are cleared at each prime and after each transition.
+
+The COMPLETED source-bound run reports96273 distinct matrices,96273
+five-prime cases,zero disagreements and full original mass1283675. The
+independent audit verifies the exact output against the fresh DAG/record,
+then verifies the copied replacement and mass1283075. It does not rerun
+the expensive profile enumeration. Full source/proof, physical common basis,
+new global histogram/moments and assembly must still be bound together by
+the parent before publication; these are distinct from this CRT argument.
+
+Attribution: fixed I+J projector/profile method and copied-center schedule
+icekylinx PR32/36; carrier/compiler antecedents and Paureel paid-copy interface
+retain their upstream credits. Rank-four uniform extension and h25 audit
+build on the already source-located h47 CRT audit in macro-corners.
+
+
+5. Common GL23 transfer review and publication gate
+I independently read the controls worker's complete proof
+research/nested-stream-exploration/macro-corners/fixed25-basis-compatibility.txt,
+SHA256 dc8db4b31a710191cf252a36388497c774ef396aa591877a512b1fcdfd89d999.
+Its scope is the actual reversed(23,25) prescription R=[I,22,I],C=[I,0,I],
+not a dimension substitution in the older(45,47) constants. At25 the fixed
+triple products are68/39 inside and-5/26 outside, all nonzero and normalized.
+The new complements' explicit normalized pair
+ p'=e_i+(17/4)1, xi'=(8/39)1^t-4e_i^t
+has every coordinate nonzero. These identities are consistent with H=I-J/9
+and L25=I+J; they add no requirement that L25 vary generically.
+
+The actual first23/last23 corner of A tensor(v nu) is diagonally scaled A
+with nonzero FIXED middle scales, so generic first-axis local patterns retain
+their proof on GL23. The first25/last25 corner of(p xi) tensor B is diagonally
+scaled B, with scales from generic first-axis coordinates. This is enough to
+transfer the entire fixed B profile: the selected corner has rank rank(B),
+which is already the rank of the complete ambient tensor projector. Ordered
+elimination finds that complete rank in the first25 rows and last25 columns;
+no extra outside pivot can remain. Diagonal row/column scaling preserves all
+ordered zero and nonzero minors. Paid ordered-affine wrappers and the width
+children are still the inherited compiler's costs, not free coordinate moves.
+The exterior rank-complement/middle-identity decompositions remain the same.
+
+The data proof correctly separates universal zeros from specialization:
+all-weight reversed23 rank-cut identities supply zeros, while its exhaustive
+2300 second-axis triple witnesses at the admissible prime1000003 establish
+nonzero rational prefix minors. These finite witnesses are one-sided exact
+nonvanishing statements and do not need a CRT argument. They must not be
+used to infer universal zeros; the proof explicitly does not do that. The
+actual nullity47, offset3 and physical21/17/middle481 blocks are retained.
+
+For EACH fixed first triple projector and fixed second triple, transitivity
+of GL23 on rank-one idempotents allows the exhibited first-axis witness.
+This proves the corresponding minor is a nonzero rational function on the
+SAME GL23 family; it does not require one witness point to work for every
+first triple at once. Generic first-axis ordinary-profile and scale
+conditions are also nonzero functions on that family. Their finite product
+is nonzero on irreducible GL23, so one rational basis satisfies every
+physical condition. The fixed middle profile supplies constants, not new
+polynomials to impose on GL23. The copied complement additions are already
+covered by their fixed exact rank-one matrices and the same scale condition.
+No hidden generic-L25 or separately chosen per-motif basis is required.
+
+Publication gate: PASS for this specific mathematical transfer, subject to
+binding the actual source-hashed completed profile, common-basis certificate,
+new global moment/arithmetic certificate and inherited proof dependencies in
+the package. The current audit did not regenerate the complete scalar DAG or
+profile independently; it parsed the fresh source DAG, derived and checked
+the CRT bound and counts, and inspected the reconstruction/common-basis
+arguments. Those evidence boundaries should remain explicit. No full all-size
+compiler/analytic theorem, global optimum, or new numerical kappa is asserted
+by this audit. Later competitors such as PR38 do not change this proof gate;
+live numerical comparison is a separate parent task.
